          <p>Winnetka's Tudor Revival and Colonial estates in zip code {zipCodes} were built 1890s–1940s with hand-pressed decorative brick, limestone accents, and lime-based mortar that can't be matched with standard Portland blends. Cook County's 90+ freeze-thaw cycles and direct Lake Michigan moisture exposure make these joints fail faster than any inland property — mortar must match the original in composition and color or the damage is visible and permanent.</p>
          <p>Many Winnetka properties in Cook County require HOA or landmark board documentation before any repair can begin. All Masonry Services provides mortar sample testing, material specs, and written scope for board submission — plus a free estimate before any work starts. Tuckpointing, chimney restoration, and limestone repair handled correctly from the first joint.</p>
